      "mergedPostDetails": "What happens:\n\nAfter launching, joining worlds works fine at first. After a later world join, every player's voice becomes choppy/chopped up for me, and other players report that I sound choppy too. It stays broken in every world afterward, including worlds that worked earlier in the session, until I fully restart VRChat.\n\nSteps to reproduce (from attached log):\n\n1. Launch VRChat → Home\n\n2. Join World A (Midnight Rooftop): voice fine\n\n3. Join World B (The Black Cat): voice fine\n\n4. Join World C (The Mafia Bar): voice choppy\n\n5. Rejoin World A: still choppy\n\n6. Restart VRChat → fixed\n\nObservations:\n\n- Debug menu shows 0 Loss by CRC Check, 0 Loss by Challenge, round trip variance ~5, Suffering 0. The network is clean.\n\n- In the Players debug panel, Intrvl Q turns red for almost every player once the problem starts (mostly green/yellow before).\n\n- In the log, the join where it broke shows \"LocalPlayerObject is null, retrying in 2 seconds\" (22:18:46). Right after that, departing players start being \"Moved to recovery list\". This doesn't happen in the earlier worlds, and on leaving World C every player was moved to the recovery list.\n\n- Not hardware-related: other apps sound fine, and a VRChat restart fixes it every time.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[2026.4.1p2-1938] Voice becomes choppy (incoming + outgoing) after a later world join, persists until restart. No packet loss",
